      "writtenOn": "2023-04-19T23:43:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "does INIT_I2C make sense? in modern cros-ec, we set up I2C before\nhooks, so this hasn\u0027t been necessary for a long time. does\nzephyr behave differently? if we really need to wait for\nI2C to be initialized to access CBI,\nshouldn\u0027t this be INIT_I2C+1?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 63,
        "startChar": 35,
        "endLine": 63,
        "endChar": 53
      },
      "revId": "9a36ba83cc0d0ba989ca69e90a1d2a0832b7ffca",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5e16f4bc_dbc0b847",
        "filename": "zephyr/program/rex/rex/src/usb_mux_config.c",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 63,
      "author": {
        "id": 1541242
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-04-20T12:56:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The code inside the method deals with gpio pin initialization, and modifications to what is configured in device tree. They are better to be modified before any other step based on CBI value. I also see other zephyr projects doing the similar way.",
      "parentUuid": "f88fd35e_4c6fd755",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 63,
        "startChar": 35,
        "endLine": 63,
        "endChar": 53
      },
      "revId": "9a36ba83cc0d0ba989ca69e90a1d2a0832b7ffca",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "94810eca_32935145",
        "filename": "zephyr/program/rex/rex/src/usb_mux_config.c",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 63,
      "author": {
        "id": 1190764
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-04-25T02:48:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "when does zephyr enable I2C? in cros-ec, it\u0027s done before any init,\nso you don\u0027t need to defer to INIT_I2C.",
      "parentUuid": "5e16f4bc_dbc0b847",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 63,
        "startChar": 35,
        "endLine": 63,
        "endChar": 53
      },
      "revId": "9a36ba83cc0d0ba989ca69e90a1d2a0832b7ffca",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "45daf12d_3d299e12",
        "filename": "zephyr/program/rex/rex/src/usb_mux_config.c",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 63,
      "author": {
        "id": 1541242
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-04-25T15:11:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "As per response from Diana, seems like I2C_INIT happens first, then I2C_INIT PRIO to pick proper drivers and configuration, then I2C_INIT POST, based on CL ID : 1772490",
      "parentUuid": "94810eca_32935145",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 63,
        "startChar": 35,
        "endLine": 63,
        "endChar": 53
      },
      "revId": "9a36ba83cc0d0ba989ca69e90a1d2a0832b7ffca",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d00d135f_f9365c46",
        "filename": "zephyr/program/rex/rex/src/usb_mux_config.c",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 63,
      "author": {
        "id": 1190764
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-04-25T19:03:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "that patch moves the i2c_init() from `HOOK_PRIO_INIT_I2C`\nto before hooks run. INIT_I2C was intended to initialize i2c,\nso that\u0027s not the right hook to use if the intent is to\nwait for i2c to be ready for execution.\nbrya uses `HOOK_PRIO_INIT_CHIPSET` which happens to be the same\nas `HOOK_PRIO_POST_I2C`. either is fine with me.",
      "parentUuid": "45daf12d_3d299e12",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 63,
        "startChar": 35,
        "endLine": 63,
        "endChar": 53
      },
